# oj-paths.env - per-key state-path overrides, read by `oj-helper resolve-path`.
#
# Values are WORKSPACE-RELATIVE and must include the `.claude/` prefix:
# `retros=.claude/history/retros` resolves inside the state tree, while
# `retros=history/retros` resolves OUTSIDE it. resolve-path warns on the second
# form and honors it anyway, so read the warning rather than ignoring it. An
# absolute value is honored silently, as a deliberate escape.
#
# `#` comments and surrounding whitespace are allowed. For any key, the LAST
# assignment wins.

# --- layout profile --------------------------------------------------------
# `hierarchy` gives the six category keys type-based defaults in one line,
# rather than six overrides that can drift out of agreement:
#   decisions      -> .claude/decisions.md
#   open-questions -> .claude/open-questions.md
#   facts          -> .claude/facts/
#   requirements | design | plan -> <node>/<type>.md
#
# Deeper nodes are addressed per call rather than configured here:
#   oj-helper resolve-path design --node [PROJECT_NODE]/[SUBJECT]
#
# Remove this line to return to `flat` (the default). Nothing else needs to
# change: the plugin keeps no state about the profile and re-reads it per call.
layout=hierarchy

# --- the backlog is plural under this profile ------------------------------
# One backlog per owning node. `**` spans directory levels, and several
# whitespace-separated patterns are allowed because the files making up one
# backlog need not share a filename.
#
# ANCHOR EACH PATTERN AT A NODE. A bare `.claude/**/plan.md` also matches
# archived plans under a history area, silently pulling retired work into every
# listing. Add a pattern when a new top-level node is created - that is the
# intended maintenance point.
#
# Read the set with `oj-helper backlog-list` (aggregates); write with
# `oj-helper resolve-path backlog`.
backlog-glob=.claude/backlog.md .claude/[PROJECT_NODE]/**/backlog.md .claude/[PROJECT_NODE]/**/plan.md

# --- deliberately NOT set --------------------------------------------------
# artifacts: under this profile there is no dump directory by design - a
# document goes to the node that owns the subject, in the file named for its
# type. Setting this re-creates the folder the taxonomy exists to remove, and
# the skills will fill it. Leave it unset so the filing rule resolves a TYPE
# key instead.
#
# id-index: override-only, no default under any profile. Set it only if this
# project authors a real id -> owning-file index file. Until then
# `oj-helper backlog-lint` is what guards id uniqueness across the set.

# --- optional relocations --------------------------------------------------
# Uncomment if this project keeps retrospectives somewhere other than the
# default `.claude/archive/retros`.
# retros=.claude/history/retros
